Input: {"question": "In which significant event was Dynamic utilization of condensing metadata involved?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 56, "text": "**Dynamic Utilization of Condensing Metadata in Filing**"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 58, "end": 193, "text": "The dynamic utilization of condensing metadata played a crucial role in a significant event filing, as evidenced by US Patent 11356539."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 194, "end": 332, "text": "This article provides a comprehensive overview of the concept, its application, and the evidence supporting its involvement in the filing."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 333, "end": 386, "text": "**What is Dynamic Utilization of Condensing Metadata?"}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 387, "end": 389, "text": "**"}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 391, "end": 566, "text": "Dynamic utilization of condensing metadata refers to the process of efficiently managing and processing metadata in a way that optimizes data storage, retrieval, and analysis."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 567, "end": 741, "text": "Metadata, which is \"data that provides information about other data,\" is condensed into a more compact and meaningful form, enabling faster and more accurate data processing."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 742, "end": 917, "text": "This approach is particularly useful in applications where large amounts of data need to be handled, such as in data warehousing, cloud computing, and artificial intelligence."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 918, "end": 943, "text": "**Application in Filing**"}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 945, "end": 1109, "text": "In the context of filing, dynamic utilization of condensing metadata enables the efficient management of large volumes of documents, data, and other digital assets."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1110, "end": 1280, "text": "By condensing metadata, filing systems can quickly identify, categorize, and retrieve relevant information, reducing the time and effort required for document management."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1281, "end": 1317, "text": "**Evidence from US Patent 11356539**"}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1319, "end": 1454, "text": "US Patent 11356539, granted on June 14, 2022, provides conclusive evidence of the dynamic utilization of condensing metadata in filing."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1455, "end": 1661, "text": "The patent, titled \"System and Method for Efficient Data Management,\" describes a novel approach to data management that involves the condensing of metadata to facilitate faster data retrieval and analysis."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1662, "end": 1803, "text": "According to the patent, the system uses a metadata condenser to reduce the size of metadata, making it more efficient to store and transmit."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1804, "end": 1941, "text": "The condensed metadata is then used to facilitate rapid data retrieval, enabling users to quickly locate and access relevant information."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1942, "end": 1962, "text": "**Credible Sources**"}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1964, "end": 1997, "text": "* US Patent and Trademark Office."}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1998, "end": 2005, "text": "(2022)."}, "D1S20": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2006, "end": 2054, "text": "System and Method for Efficient Data Management."}, "D1S21": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2055, "end": 2074, "text": "US Patent 11356539."}, "D1S22": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2075, "end": 2122, "text": "* National Archives and Records Administration."}, "D1S23": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2123, "end": 2130, "text": "(n.d.)."}, "D1S24": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2131, "end": 2150, "text": "Metadata Standards."}, "D1S25": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2151, "end": 2218, "text": "Retrieved from <https:\\/\\/www.archives.gov\\/records-mgmt\\/metadata>"}, "D1S26": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2219, "end": 2268, "text": "* International Organization for Standardization."}, "D1S27": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2269, "end": 2276, "text": "(2019)."}, "D1S28": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2277, "end": 2374, "text": "ISO\\/IEC 11179-1:2019 - Information technology -- Metadata registries (MDR) -- Part 1: Framework."}, "D1S29": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2375, "end": 2435, "text": "Retrieved from <https:\\/\\/www.iso.org\\/standard\\/72251.html>"}, "D1S30": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2437, "end": 2451, "text": "**Conclusion**"}, "D1S31": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2453, "end": 2582, "text": "The dynamic utilization of condensing metadata played a significant role in the filing event, as evidenced by US Patent 11356539."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 59, "text": "Dynamic Utilization of Condensing Metadata and Royal Assent"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 61, "end": 265, "text": "The dynamic utilization of condensing metadata, a patented technology (US Patent 11356539), has been implicated in the significant event of royal assent, a formal approval of a proposed law in monarchies."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 266, "end": 288, "text": "History of Involvement"}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 290, "end": 515, "text": "The first recorded instance of dynamic utilization of condensing metadata in royal assent dates back to 2010, when the British monarch, Queen Elizabeth II, granted royal assent to the Constitutional Reform and Governance Act."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 516, "end": 752, "text": "A study published in the Journal of Legislative Studies in 2012 revealed that the Queen's advisors had employed the technology to streamline the approval process, reducing the time taken to review and approve the legislation by 30% (1)."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 753, "end": 785, "text": "Further Research and Development"}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 787, "end": 965, "text": "In the following years, researchers at the University of Cambridge conducted a series of studies on the application of dynamic utilization of condensing metadata in royal assent."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 966, "end": 1169, "text": "Their findings, published in the Cambridge Law Journal in 2015, demonstrated that the technology improved the accuracy of legislative reviews by 25% and reduced the workload of royal advisors by 40% (2)."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1170, "end": 1187, "text": "Notable Instances"}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1189, "end": 1347, "text": "One notable instance of dynamic utilization of condensing metadata in royal assent was during the passage of the Scottish Independence Referendum Act in 2014."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1348, "end": 1508, "text": "The Scottish Government's use of the technology enabled the rapid review and approval of the legislation, allowing the referendum to take place on schedule (3)."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1509, "end": 1612, "text": "Another significant example is the royal assent granted to the European Union (Withdrawal) Act in 2018."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1613, "end": 1784, "text": "The UK Parliament's use of dynamic utilization of condensing metadata facilitated the swift passage of the legislation, ensuring a timely exit from the European Union (4)."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1785, "end": 1795, "text": "References"}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1797, "end": 1810, "text": "(1) Smith, J."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1811, "end": 1818, "text": "(2012)."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1819, "end": 1922, "text": "\"The Role of Technology in Royal Assent: A Case Study of the Constitutional Reform and Governance Act.\""}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1923, "end": 1970, "text": "Journal of Legislative Studies, 18(2), 123-145."}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1971, "end": 2002, "text": "(2) Johnson, K., & Thompson, R."}, "D2S20": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2003, "end": 2010, "text": "(2015)."}, "D2S21": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2011, "end": 2108, "text": "\"Dynamic Utilization of Condensing Metadata in Royal Assent: A Study of Efficiency and Accuracy.\""}, "D2S22": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2109, "end": 2147, "text": "Cambridge Law Journal, 74(2), 251-275."}, "D2S23": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2148, "end": 2172, "text": "(3) Scottish Government."}, "D2S24": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2173, "end": 2180, "text": "(2014)."}, "D2S25": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2181, "end": 2249, "text": "\"Scottish Independence Referendum Act: Review and Approval Process.\""}, "D2S26": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2250, "end": 2281, "text": "Edinburgh: Scottish Government."}, "D2S27": {"document_number": 2, "doc